@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

@* Hero (plan 2.2): answers "what", "where", and "how to book" on the first screen.
   aria-labelledby names the section after its headline for screen-reader landmark lists. *@
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    @* Decorative photo (alt="": the headline carries the meaning). It's an <img>, not a CSS
       background, so the browser finds it in the HTML straight away; fetchpriority="high" because
       it's the largest thing on the first screen (Largest Contentful Paint). width/height reserve
       its space before it loads.
       Photo: Edward Muntinga on Unsplash (https://unsplash.com/photos/CjX9rtKsW8E), Unsplash License
       (free commercial use, no attribution required). Resized to 1920px wide. *@
    <img class="hero-image" src="@Assets["images/hero-massage.jpg"]" alt=""
         width="1920" height="1282" fetchpriority="high" />

    <div class="hero-content">
        <h1 id="hero-heading" class="hero-heading">Therapeutic massage for recovery, pain relief, and performance</h1>
        <p class="hero-subheading">Registered massage therapy in Guelph, Ontario</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            @* Both booking buttons point at the contact form until online booking exists (plan 4.1). *@
            <a class="btn btn-lg btn-accent" href="contact">Book an appointment</a>
            <a class="btn btn-lg btn-outline-light" href="services">View services</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
